  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"4.1.22\"\n\npackage:\n  name: softsusy\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BAllanach/softsusy/v${{ version }}/tags/softsusy-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 2584e8f8ddd2c7069e7f5f5f4c38a903daa9d8dbbb92256adc548547377e2e89\n  patches:\n    # c.f. https://github.com/BAllanach/softsusy/pull/42\n    - fix-duplicate-tsil-header.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  skip:\n    - win\n\nrequirements:\n  run_exports:\n    - ${{ pin_subpackage(\"softsusy\", upper_bound=\"x.x\") }}\n  build:\n    - ${{ stdlib(\"c\") }}\n    - ${{ compiler(\"c\") }}\n    - ${{ compiler(\"cxx\") }}\n    - ${{ compiler(\"fortran\") }}\n    - automake\n    - libtool\n    - make\n    - sed\n    - grep\n    - pkg-config\n    - gnuconfig\n\ntests:\n  - package_contents:\n      strict: true\n      bin:\n        - softsusy.x\n        - softsusy-nmssm.x\n        - softpoint.x\n        - rpvsoftsusy.x\n        - rpvneut.x\n      lib:\n        - soft\n        - supermodel\n        - tsil\n      include:\n        - softsusy/*.h\n      files:\n        - share/softsusy/*\n  - script:\n      - softsusy.x\n      - softsusy-nmssm.x\n      - rpvsoftsusy.x\n      - rpvneut.x\n      - softpoint.x sugra --m0=1000 --m12=1000 --a0=0 --tanBeta=10 --sgnMu=1\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://softsusy.hepforge.org/\n  repository: https://github.com/BAllanach/softsusy\n  documentation: https://softsusy.hepforge.org/html/\n  license: GPL-3.0-or-later\n  license_file:\n    - README.md\n    - src/Himalaya-1.0.0/LICENSE\n  summary: Calculates supersymmetric particle spectra\n  description: |\n    This program provides a SUSY spectrum in the NMSSM, or the MSSM including\n    flavour violation and with or without R-parity consistent with input\n    Standard Model fermion mass/mixings and electroweak/strong coupling data.\n    The R-parity violating mode can calculate neutrino masses and mixings to\n    1 loop.\n    SOFTSUSY can be used in conjunction with other programs for many different\n    particle physics calculations.\n    SOFTSUSY now has a mode with 3 loop RGEs and some 2-loop threshold\n    correction and 2-loop SUSY QCD corrections to gluino and squark pole masses.\n    SOFTSUSY now computes decay branching ratios for the MSSM and NMSSM.\n    It also ships with (and links to) Himalaya-1.0 for three-loop corrections\n    to mh0.\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - matthewfeickert\n",
